 "notes": [
  "No objectives beyond killing units (survey 005).",
  "Portina Brook is 14 river hexes in one piece: 1,0 2,1 3,1 4,2 4,3 4,4 4,5 4,6 4,7 5,7 5,8 6,9 7,9 8,10. It has no bridge or ford field: it is a fordable stream that stops movement but costs no dice (survey rule and R. Borg ruling); rulings research decides how the engine maps that.",
  "Hill 2,0 with fieldworks: BR/FA starts on it. The block hides most of the works. Faint hill rays surround the block and a brown sandbag edge shows below it running from the south-west corner to the south-east corner, so sides are recorded as SW, SE and E. DOUBT: the block hides the E wall. 006 shows the same three-sided works art (W+SW+SE on 2,4; SW+SE+E on 2,5); here no W wall shows left of the block while the left end of the V is visible, so the hidden vertical wall is taken to be on the E side. The 21 plain hills in the survey count are the other hill hexes; 2,0 is the survey's 'hill with entrenchment'.",
  "Hills under unit blocks (1,7 1,8 1,9 2,8 3,4 3,5 3,6 7,4 7,5 7,6 7,7 7,8) read from the rays around the blocks and scan.py (0.13-0.18).",
  "Leaders: Sherbrooke (1,1), Mackenzie (1,5) and Hill (1,8) stand alone; Ruffin (7,7 with FR/LN), Sebastiani (8,2 with FR/LN), Merlin (8,11 with FR/LC). The booklet's King Joseph, Jourdan, Victor are not on the map (survey discrepancy 7). Map title reads 'Talavera (French attack on British)' (discrepancy 12)."
 ]
